{"requirements":[{"id":"minimum-password-length","requirement":"New user passwords must be at least 12 characters long.","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"The persistent policy specifies minlen=12, and pwscore rejects an 11-character password before and after restart. However, two direct password-setting probes created a user and successfully assigned an 11-character password through chpasswd and passwd --stdin (rc=0). Thus the configured quality rule was not demonstrated as an enforced password-change requirement and was directly bypassed in the tested administrative paths.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7e71e30e121045c6","cmd-550dbf218a9f4636","cmd-9476f109bc7b49d6","cmd-32b3301e25964f98","cmd-cae16fdfe89045b9"]},{"id":"minimum-character-classes","requirement":"New user passwords must contain at least three different character classes.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"The persistent policy specifies minclass=3, both PAM password stacks reference pam_pwquality, and pwscore rejects a 16-character one-class password before and after restart while accepting a four-class password. No actual password-setting probe attempted a one-class password, so enforcement through the user password-change path remains unproven.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7e71e30e121045c6","cmd-550dbf218a9f4636","cmd-9476f109bc7b49d6"]}],"confidence":0.91,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The policy-file creation directly served the task. The temporary-user/password mutations were bounded enforcement probes and were fully cleaned up. The reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol. Final observations show no failed services, no probe artifacts in the bounded temporary-file inventory, unchanged socket exposure apart from post-reboot process identities, and healthy package-manager state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7e71e30e121045c6","cmd-32b3301e25964f98","cmd-cae16fdfe89045b9","cmd-550dbf218a9f4636","cmd-430c770519e84bb2","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The requested policy was persistently configured and its libpwquality checks survived restart, but the minimum-length requirement was not actually enforced by either tested system password-setting command. Character-class validation works in the policy engine but lacks an end-to-end password-change test. The node-restart evidence protocol was complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the reboot was acknowledged, the boot identity changed consistently with the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and system, SSH, policy, and failed-unit state recovered.","limitations":["No non-root interactive password-change attempt was captured, so the evidence cannot determine whether ordinary users are blocked even though both tested root-driven password-setting paths accepted the short password.","No end-to-end password-setting attempt used a sufficiently long password with fewer than three character classes; character-class enforcement is demonstrated only through pwscore and configuration.","The restart protocol demonstrates recovered system, SSH, and policy state; no separate application data or cluster workload existed in the supplied single-node task evidence."]}
